	<div class="fsElement fsPostElement fsList fsThumbnailRectangle fsThumbnailLarge fsItemCount_15" id="fsEl_2268" data-use-new="true" data-board-id="2" data-overwrite-title="" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
		<div class="fsListItems">

<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-2 fsTag-2 fsTag-105 fsTag-111 fsTag-137" data-post-id="2564" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_2268_2564">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="buusd-home/post/a-message-from-the-superintendent" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/a-message-from-the-superintendent"><div data-aspect-ratio="0.5450204638472033" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1466}]" class="fsCroppedImage" title="Message from the Superintendent Thumbnail"><img data-aspect-ratio="0.5450204638472033" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_4/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1790185989/bsuvtorg/z1lc8ehnhwf0n8nd4gqq/Message-from-Supt-Thumbnail.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1466}]" alt="Message from the Superintendent Thumbnail" class="fsStyleSROnly" /></div></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_2268_2564">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="buusd-home/post/a-message-from-the-superintendent" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/a-message-from-the-superintendent">
			A Message from the Superintendent
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>Dear Barre Community,</p>

<p>Thank you to the many voices that showed up and shared their perspectives at the Board meeting on Monday night. Details or a recording of that meeting can be viewed at&nbsp;<a href="http://www.buusd.org/district/board" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.buusd.org/district/board</a>.</p>

<p>The Board will meet again on October 5, 2026 to discuss the next draft of the budget (vote four) and to continue to discuss the operation of the district without a voter approved budget. We hope to have another budget for a vote in late October. We will share this date as soon as it is set.</p>

<p>We are continuing to work with the State of Vermont and the Agency of Education on our current operations plan to continue running schools without an approved budget. Please see their guidance memo attached to this letter that was released after our meeting with Secretary Saunders and her team on Monday. The conversations around temporary cuts to our operations (co-curriculars, athletics, staff, transportation, supplies, building projects, etc) are ongoing and are a result of needing to operate on 87% of last year&#39;s budget until we have a budget.</p>

<p>To operate on 87% for the full school year we would need to reduce costs by $8.4 million dollars. There are not $8.4 million dollars of cuts available to us in BUUSD and we have communicated that reality to the State. The total of all possible cuts, many of which are untenable, are at least five million dollars short of that goal. We know that this has been uncomfortable, but we have had to discuss all of the options. We know that this has been upsetting to many, as activities are an essential part of our programming. It is our goal to work towards another budget vote and move past the current operating restrictions that have been placed on us by Vermont law.</p>

<p>There are no plans to include cuts to student activities, co-curriculars, or sports programs in budget draft four. Those are not items the Board or administration want to remove from our budget proposal for the school year. We heard the voices that spoke at the meeting, and our business office is working to analyze many of the suggestions that we heard from board and community members as we work on the next draft of the budget.</p>

<p>There is a lot of misinformation circulating, and we encourage families to rely on official communication channels to understand the differences between operating on 87% of last year&#39;s budget and any reductions that the Board may consider for budget vote four.</p>

<p>Please know that we understand that these are painful conversations for many in our school community. It is our goal to inform you of the current situation as best we can, while navigating the uncharted waters we find ourselves in. Thank you for your passion and your support of our students.</p>

<p><a href="https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v1790088441/bsuvtorg/oqkrfqbu13coedgcrf0v/AOEMemo_WhatHappensWhenaSchoolBudgetDoesntPassFall2026.pdf" target="_blank">Here</a> is a link to a memo from the Agency of Education regarding what happens when a school budget does not pass.</p>

<p>Sincerely,<br />
Emilie Knisley<br />
Superintendent of Schools</p>

		</div>




</article>
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-2" data-post-id="2561" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_2268_2561">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="buusd-home/post/free-back-to-school-celebration-playing-fields-september-8" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/free-back-to-school-celebration-playing-fields-september-8"><div data-aspect-ratio="1.5" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200}]" class="fsCroppedImage" title="Playing Fields Performance Flyer - Outdoor Performance"><img data-aspect-ratio="1.5" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1788881550/bsuvtorg/z6xtu2qn8fap4bzp8njr/PlayingFields-2026-Flyers-Barre.jpg&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200}]" alt="Playing Fields Performance Flyer - Outdoor Performance" class="fsStyleSROnly" /></div></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_2268_2561">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="buusd-home/post/free-back-to-school-celebration-playing-fields-september-8" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/free-back-to-school-celebration-playing-fields-september-8">
			Free Back to School Celebration &quot;Playing Fields&quot; September 8
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>Join us on September 8th at 6:00pm for the Playing Fields Project at Flynn Elementary School! This free back-to-school celebration is presented by The Flynn and Barre City Elementary and Middle School.&nbsp;</p>

<p>This year, bring your friends and family for an awe-inspiring evening of large-scale puppetry, featuring&nbsp;Sea Fantasy &ndash; The Pearl. The show is created by Plasticiens Volants, an exciting and dynamic street theater troupe joining us all the way from France.</p>

		</div>




</article>
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-2" data-post-id="2540" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_2268_2540">

	<a class="fsThumbnail fsPostLink " data-slug="buusd-home/post/special-services-community-forum-may-13" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/special-services-community-forum-may-13"><div data-aspect-ratio="0.525" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200}]" class="fsCroppedImage" title="Special Services Community Forum Flyer"><img data-aspect-ratio="0.525" data-image-sizes="[{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_1/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:256},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_2/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:512},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto,t_image_size_3/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:800},{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://resources.finalsite.net/images/f_auto,q_auto/v1778603419/bsuvtorg/ct8efrqrjxm1pgebg4mi/SpecialServicesCommunityForum.png&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:1200}]" alt="Special Services Community Forum Flyer" class="fsStyleSROnly" /></div></a>

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_2268_2540">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="buusd-home/post/special-services-community-forum-may-13" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/special-services-community-forum-may-13">
			Special Services Community Forum - May 13
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p>The BUUSD Special Services Team invites you to attend their community forum on Wednesday, May 13. Join them to learn about a review of the 25/26 school year and hear more information about Extended School Year (ESY) 2026.</p>

<p>When: Wednesday, May 13<br />
Time: 5-6:30pm<br />
Where: Spaulding High School Library<br />
Virtual: meet.google.com/kdq-ghbt-fto<br />
Phone: 515-518-4723 PIN: 221 499 531#</p>

		</div>




</article>
<article class="fsStyleAutoclear fsBoard-2" data-post-id="2518" data-authenticated-comments="true" aria-labelledby="fsArticle_2268_2518">

	

		
		<div class="fsTitle " id="fsArticle_2268_2518">
		<a class="fsPostLink" data-slug="buusd-home/post/a-message-to-the-barre-community-regarding-the-school-budget-vote" data-opens-in="page" data-page-id="1308" href="https://www.buusd.org/district/bsu-news/story/~board/buusd-home/post/a-message-to-the-barre-community-regarding-the-school-budget-vote">
			A Message to the Barre Community Regarding the School Budget Vote
</a></div>

	







		<div class="fsSummary">
			<p><span style="font-size:10.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#1f1f1f"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">Dear Parents, Caregivers, Neighbors and Community Members,</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="line-height:1.8857142857142857; background-color:#ffffff; padding:0pt 0pt 9pt 0pt"><span style="font-size:10.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#1f1f1f"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">I want to express my sincere appreciation to everyone who participated in the recent school budget vote. Whether you cast your ballot at the polls or through an absentee process, your engagement is vital to the health and future of our community.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

<p style="line-height:1.8857142857142857; background-color:#ffffff; padding:0pt 0pt 9pt 0pt"><span style="font-size:10.5pt; font-variant:normal; white-space:pre-wrap"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="color:#1f1f1f"><span style="font-weight:400"><span style="font-style:normal"><span style="text-decoration:none">While we are disappointed that the proposed FY27 budget was not approved, we hear the community&rsquo;s concerns regarding affordability and sustainability.&nbsp; We recognize that external pressures&mdash;including significant changes in student demographics, rising health insurance premiums, and a substantial decrease in our long-term weighted average daily membership&mdash;have created a complex financial landscape for both the district and our taxpayers. <a data-file-name="AMessagetotheBarreCommunityRegardingtheSchoolBudgetVote.pdf" data-resource-uuid="bc434a54-6956-4710-ad3b-074a4b91700a" href="/fs/resource-manager/view/bc434a54-6956-4710-ad3b-074a4b91700a" target="_blank">(Click to Read More)&nbsp;</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>

		</div>




</article>
